            {
              "n": 1,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "# H18: shared Mind/Type adaptation preparation"
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "Status: source implemented and CPU tested; independent parent review gates pending."
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "Scope: deterministic data/contract readiness audit and disabled experiment specification."
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "This phase neither trains nor qualifies a learned model."
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "## Resolved choices"
            },
            {
              "n": 8,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 9,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "Retain one pinned Qwen3-VL-2B multimodal base. First compare its unchanged behavior"
            },
            {
              "n": 10,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "under task-specific Mind and Type prompts. If suitable new data and evidence justify"
            },
            {
              "n": 11,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "adaptation, propose one rank-4 multitask LoRA on that shared base. Separate adapters"
            },
            {
              "n": 12,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "require a later measured deficit, suitable data, and a demonstrated gain large enough"
            },
            {
              "n": 13,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "to justify residency, serving and maintenance costs. No split-adapter work is authorized"
            },
            {
              "n": 14,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "here. The current 58-row artifact is inventory evidence, not the proposed training set."
            },
            {
              "n": 15,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 16,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "## Acceptance and evidence"
            },
            {
              "n": 17,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 18,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "- [x] Audit original frozen source allocations, candidate rows, all media hashes/rights,"
            },
            {
              "n": 19,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "  family/language counts, source identities and exact original prompts/first actions."
            },
            {
              "n": 20,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "- [x] Distinguish pixel/window logical actions from normalized point outputs and bound"
            },
            {
              "n": 21,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "  Mind plans. Report English-only coverage and unqualified Arabic rendering."
            },
            {
              "n": 22,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "- [x] Recompute H14 per-family/language outcomes from frozen tasks and raw outputs;"
            },
            {
              "n": 23,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "  enforce its training exclusion and report H15's limited engineering evidence."
            },
            {
              "n": 24,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "- [x] Reject altered rows even with updated JSONL hashes, relabeled heldouts/languages,"
            }
